<h2 id=3D"implementation">Implementation</h2>
<p>Note that in Python, heaps are min-heaps by default. To mimic the functi=
onality of a max-heap, we can insert numbers as negatives in the <code>left=
_half</code> heap. This way, the largest original value becomes the smalles=
t when negated, positioning it at the top of the heap. When we retrieve a v=
alue from this heap, we multiply it by -1 to get its original value.</p>
